invariant: INV-17
file: src/quic_keys.c
catches: quic_suite_test
reason: quic_keys_init_suite does not wipe the set's stored powers before it
  keys, so a set keyed under ChaCha20, or under a ch_cfg.cpu without
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES, after an AES-GCM key keeps the powers of that
  key's hash subkey. No packet reads them there, so every packet is right.
  bin/quic_suite_test keys one set that way and requires 256 zero bytes
  (test/ghash_powers_tests.h, docs/decisions.md 234).

--- old
    ct_wipe(k->schedule, sizeof k->schedule);
    ct_wipe(k->ghash_powers, sizeof k->ghash_powers);
--- new
    ct_wipe(k->schedule, sizeof k->schedule);
